methods.test_03_authenticate_login_to_retrieve_t:
Authenticate Login to retrieve temporary access_token -> Use the "email": "admin@example.com" and "password": "admin123", but do not include mode and otp. Also Retrieve the access_token from the response;
Create a new folder -> Use the above retrieved access_token as bearer token, Use a random alphabetical string to provide as an input to the folder name, but don't include parent option in the payload, Retrieve the ID from the response;
Update a folder -> Use the above retrieved access_token as bearer token, Use a random alphabetical string to provide as an input to the folder name, but don't include parent option in the payload -> Validate that the response has ID which is as same as above retrieved ID, and the folder name has changed to the one which has been input in this step only.
Get the list of folder names -> Use the above retrieved access_token as bearer token -> Validate that the response has a record with the above generated and retrieved ID along with the above used folder name in step 3;
Delete a folder using folder id -> Use the above retrieved access_token as bearer token -> Use  the same above retrieved ID  to delete in this request;
Get the list of folder names -> Use the above retrieved access_token as bearer token -> Validate that the response NOT included with the record having above created folder name in step 2 , NOT even in Step 3 along with retrived ID, if it is existing by chance then throw with an appropriate error

